  message: "PR #2354 (stable-id v19, 2026-11-23/24), jsts agent commit 4a0b62b8f (on the PR branch as 0fc3c7f6e): a JS/TS callable now labels its locals' scope chain by name plus its own hashed signature. Effect on this item:\n- Point 1 (callbacks in a getter and its setter): fixed by that commit per its message (\"A getter and its setter need no word: the setter takes one parameter\"). Drafting-agent probe on the PR tip 3269081cf, locals sweep fixture ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/v19_11232026/residuals/probes/mixed/js_sweep.js: the two `function h` locals of `get p()` and `set p(v)` now have distinct stable ids (hgstableid19:6a4a6c9cf21b8c5b, :7f61055c10097543). Callbacks (not named locals) in the getter/setter pair were not re-run by the drafting agent.\n- Point 4 (computed-name methods) stands: locals of computed- or string-keyed methods are still tied (\"no name is read for them\").\n- New still-tied forms the commit lists: locals of two anonymous callbacks (two it(...) bodies), of two callables with one name and one signature (function s(a) declared twice), of objects assigned to member expressions (x.a = { m() {} }).\n- Measured, named-local pre-split tie groups (not _cb_*): knex 39 -> 34, hocuspocus 85 -> 85, nest/packages 103 -> 103; all groups incl. _cb_*: knex 684 -> 677, hocuspocus 213 -> 212, nest 685 -> 685. 36 remaining groups were sampled and sit in anonymous callbacks; the rest were not read.\n- Occurrence renumbering: an anonymous `_cb_*` callback's id moves when a same-named sibling with the same hashed text joins or leaves its group (knex 24 ids moved this way in 0f5db7682, hocuspocus 4).\nDetail: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/v19_11232026/jsts/RESULTS.md, jsts/commit_msgs/c5.txt, jsts/finam/.\nPoints 2 and 3 (field initializers, static blocks) were not re-checked."  # a1e8
